      "side": 1,
      "message": "Hi Kelly,\nThanks for correcting!\nExporting log_threaded_irq_wakeup_reason() would be sufficient for kernel drivers.\nIdealy, any wakeup irq should use enable_irq_wake() to inform PM core and thus log_irq_wakeup_reason() is called.\nThe corresponding IRQ handler could utilize log_threaded_irq_wakeup_reason() if its child IRQ is actually triggered.\n\nFor log_abnormal_wakeup_reason(), in my opinion, the current handling flow is sufficient: During each suspend callback stage, pm_wakeup_pending() is called to check if a wakeup source is activated.",
